      "headline": "Numerica Credit Union funds vital services for local families",
      "subhead": "A recent $380,000 donation from the Numerica Charitable Fund provides food, shelter, and care for children in need.",
      "sponsor_line": "Sponsored content from Numerica Credit Union",
      "body": "Tricia MacFarlan, executive director of Mirror Ministries, says support from the Numerica Charitable Fund helps her organization create a safe environment. \"Their support allows us to enhance the new Outreach Center and offer a warm, welcoming place for survivors to gather and heal,\" MacFarlan says.\n\nMacFarlan's organization is one of the local nonprofits Numerica Credit Union recognized in August with a $380,000 donation. These funds are part of Numerica CARES for Kids, a philanthropic initiative focused on the well-being of children and families.\n\nTo celebrate the awards, Numerica team members surprised organizations with in-person announcements and Polaroid cameras. The support reaches people through a variety of regional partners, including the Boys & Girls Club of Kootenai County and the CDA Backpack Program.\n\nThis community support is funded by Numerica members themselves. Through the Skip a Pay program, members pay a $30 fee to skip a monthly loan payment, which is then contributed to the fund. This year, the program fully funded every selected grant request.\n\nThe grants support services such as child care, mentorship programs, and educational support. The list of Spokane recipients includes Communities In Schools, Second Harvest, and Volunteers of America. Four nonprofits are also receiving their third consecutive round of $25,000 in funding as part of a multi-year pledge to deepen their impact.\n\n\"Year after year, Numerica goes above and beyond to not just give financially, but to truly partner with Family Promise to end the cycle of homelessness for families,\" says Emma Hughes, outreach and recruitment director for Family Promise.\n\nNumerica president and CEO Carla Cicero says the program is about investing in the future. \"Numerica CARES for Kids is about investing in the well-being of children and families in our communities,\" Cicero says. \"In challenging times, we've seen these incredible nonprofits wrap their arms around those who need it most. Through the Numerica Charitable Fund, we're honored to support the life-changing work they do every day.\"",
